{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794317471,"nonce":"7vDbIZ/2WLXpFpTmkH60sFz3USM=","message":"Plan agreed (user): build the direct wasm backend with nothing left out, and the fiber / browser-agents architecture must keep working. Approach: ash_wasm_emit (no LLVM, builds for wasm32) becomes a producer of the program's relocatable wasm object, replacing the LLVM shard code objects; the LLVM data object (strings, type descriptors, globals), the prelinked runtime, ash_wasm_link and its link-time fiber transform stay. Order: (1) relocatable object writer (symbols + the 12 relocation types ash_wasm_link supports) and the data-symbol contract from aot_data.rs, (2) hello-world through the real linker and ash run, (3) objects / strings / globals / natives / calls, (4) SIMD (AIR vectors are fixed 128-bit = wasm v128: add/sub/mul/div/sqrt/neg/abs/logic/select/shifts/compares/splat/convert/load/store map 1:1; i8x16.mul, i64x2 min/max and the horizontal reductions need sequences; vector Fma must stay exact via per-lane ash.fma imports; simd128 and exception-handling are already enabled for the wasm target and fiber.rs already spills v128), (5) closures, virtual dispatch, indirect calls (exact target set the fiber transform needs), (6) exceptions in the existing wasm EH convention, (7) polls and shadow frames at the same sites as the LLVM path so the fiber transform and threads-on-agents keep working. Every unsupported instruction kind falls back to the LLVM shard until the list is empty. Existing tests to reuse as differential tests: TestSimd, TestVecLanes, TestVectorize, TestVecArrayAddr, the conformance suite, aot_wasm_fibers.","files":null}]}